{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"callout","kind":"caution","title":"Caution","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This class has been deprecated and will be removed in the next major version of TanStack Router.\nPlease use the "},{"type":"link","href":"./createRootRouteFunction.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRootRoute"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function instead."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RootRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" class extends the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route"},{"type":"text","value":" class and can be used to create a root route instance. A root route instance can then be used to create a route tree."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rootroute-constructor","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RootRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" constructor"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RootRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" constructor accepts an object as its only argument."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"constructor-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constructor options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The options that will be used to configure the root route instance."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type:"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"Omit<\n  RouteOptions,\n  | 'path'\n  | 'id'\n  | 'getParentRoute'\n  | 'caseSensitive'\n  | 'parseParams'\n  | 'stringifyParams'\n>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./RouteOptionsType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RouteOptions"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"constructor-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constructor returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new "},{"type":"link","href":"./RouteType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instance."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { RootRoute, createRouter, Outlet } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst rootRoute = new RootRoute({\n  component: () => <Outlet />,\n  // ... root route options\n})\n\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ... other routes\n])\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n})","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"rootroute-constructor","text":"RootRoute constructor","level":2},{"id":"constructor-options","text":"Constructor options","level":3},{"id":"constructor-returns","text":"Constructor returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> [!CAUTION]\n> This class has been deprecated and will be removed in the next major version of TanStack Router.\n> Please use the [`createRootRoute`](./createRootRouteFunction.md) function instead.\n\nThe `RootRoute` class extends the `Route` class and can be used to create a root route instance. A root route instance can then be used to create a route tree.\n\n## `RootRoute` constructor\n\nThe `RootRoute` constructor accepts an object as its only argument.\n\n### Constructor options\n\nThe options that will be used to configure the root route instance.\n\n- Type:\n\n```tsx\nOmit<\n  RouteOptions,\n  | 'path'\n  | 'id'\n  | 'getParentRoute'\n  | 'caseSensitive'\n  | 'parseParams'\n  | 'stringifyParams'\n>\n```\n\n- [`RouteOptions`](./RouteOptionsType.md)\n- Optional\n\n## Constructor returns\n\nA new [`Route`](./RouteType.md) instance.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { RootRoute, createRouter, Outlet } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst rootRoute = new RootRoute({\n  component: () => <Outlet />,\n  // ... root route options\n})\n\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ... other routes\n])\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: RootRouteClass\ntitle: RootRoute class\n---\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> This class has been deprecated and will be removed in the next major version of TanStack Router.\n> Please use the [`createRootRoute`](./createRootRouteFunction.md) function instead.\n\nThe `RootRoute` class extends the `Route` class and can be used to create a root route instance. A root route instance can then be used to create a route tree.\n\n## `RootRoute` constructor\n\nThe `RootRoute` constructor accepts an object as its only argument.\n\n### Constructor options\n\nThe options that will be used to configure the root route instance.\n\n- Type:\n\n```tsx\nOmit<\n  RouteOptions,\n  | 'path'\n  | 'id'\n  | 'getParentRoute'\n  | 'caseSensitive'\n  | 'parseParams'\n  | 'stringifyParams'\n>\n```\n\n- [`RouteOptions`](./RouteOptionsType.md)\n- Optional\n\n## Constructor returns\n\nA new [`Route`](./RouteType.md) instance.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { RootRoute, createRouter, Outlet } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst rootRoute = new RootRoute({\n  component: () => <Outlet />,\n  // ... root route options\n})\n\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ... other routes\n])\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n})\n```\n"}
